\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
In the GLSM setting, is the hemisphere partition function $Z_{D^2}:K_0(D)\to\mathbb C$ a central-charge function for a Bridgeland stability condition on $D$, and for the grade-restriction subcategory $W_n$ are the phase quotient categories $D_{\zeta\gg0}$ and $D_{\zeta\ll0}$ related to $W_n$ by the conjectured commuting equivalences?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2016/9}{[S2]}.

